Dictation threw ReferenceError on every click
=============================================

`startEngineDictation` was declared beside `dictationControl` instead of inside it, but its body uses
that function's `textarea` and `node`:

    function startEngineDictation() {
      if (!textarea.isConnected || engineSttStop) return;   // ReferenceError: textarea is not defined
      ...
      node.textContent = "Stop dictation";

On macOS and in Chromium the click never reaches it — the webview recogniser exists, so the speech
path is taken. On WebKitGTK there is no recogniser at all, so the engine path IS the path, and it
threw on the first line every single time. An exception inside a click handler does not propagate to
the caller: the button did nothing, no dialog, no error, no transcript call. Read from the outside
that is "dictation does not work at all".

Two arguments, one call site: `startEngineDictation(textarea, node)`.

Verified by driving the shipped module in a browser with the Web Speech API removed and a stubbed
bridge whose transcript grows while dictation runs:

    before: Uncaught ReferenceError: textarea is not defined
    after : button "Stop dictation", aria-pressed true, textarea "HELLO FROM THE MICROPHONE.",
            Voice.getTranscript polled every 700 ms, and the text already in the service correctly
            skipped rather than dumped into the prompt.

diff -Naur a/resources/ui/capability-workflows.js b/resources/ui/capability-workflows.js
--- a/resources/ui/capability-workflows.js
+++ b/resources/ui/capability-workflows.js
@@ -258,7 +258,7 @@
         // command — and polling it is the only path that exists. Waiting for a probe first meant a
         // slow or unreachable endpoint turned Dictate into a dialog telling a Linux user to use
         // macOS dictation.
-        startEngineDictation();
+        startEngineDictation(textarea, node);
       }, "quiet");
       node.title = typeof recognitionConstructor() === "function" ? "Dictate text into the prompt" : "System dictation help";
       function start(Recognition) {
@@ -291,7 +291,7 @@
       return node;
     }
     let engineSttStop = null;
-    function startEngineDictation() {
+    function startEngineDictation(textarea, node) {
       if (!textarea.isConnected || engineSttStop) return;
       node.textContent = "Stop dictation";
